### Nomos Admin API - Full Setup Flow
### Run these in order to populate the graph

### ============================================================
### 1. Create IDPs
### ============================================================

### Create auth0
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/idp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "auth0",
  "issuer": "https://auth0.example.com"
}

### Create keycloak
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/idp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "keycloak",
  "issuer": "https://keycloak.internal.com/realms/main"
}

### Create cognito
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/idp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "cognito",
  "issuer": "https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/us-east-1_abc123"
}

### ============================================================
### 2. Create Apps
### ============================================================

### Create mobile-app-br
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br"
}

### Create mobile-app-co
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-co"
}

### Create internal-backoffice
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "internal-backoffice"
}

### ============================================================
### 3. Link Apps to IDPs (USES_IDP with audience)
### ============================================================

### mobile-app-br → auth0
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/mobile-app-br/idp/auth0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "mobile-br-auth0-client"
}

### mobile-app-br → keycloak (same app, different IDP)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/mobile-app-br/idp/keycloak
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "mobile-br-kc-internal"
}

### mobile-app-co → auth0
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/mobile-app-co/idp/auth0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "mobile-co-auth0-client"
}

### internal-backoffice → keycloak
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/internal-backoffice/idp/keycloak
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "backoffice-kc-client"
}

### ============================================================
### 4. Create API Proxies
### ============================================================

### Create account-service (deny by default)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/proxy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "account-service",
  "defaultPolicy": "deny"
}

### Create billing-service (allow by default)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/proxy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "billing-service",
  "defaultPolicy": "allow"
}

### Create notification-service (allow by default)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/proxy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "notification-service",
  "defaultPolicy": "allow"
}

### ============================================================
### 5. Grant Proxy Access (ACCESS_PROXY scoped by audience)
### ============================================================

### mobile-app-br (auth0 audience) → account-service
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "mobile-br-auth0-client"
}

### mobile-app-br (auth0 audience) → billing-service
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br",
  "proxyName": "billing-service",
  "audience": "mobile-br-auth0-client"
}

### mobile-app-br (keycloak audience) → account-service only
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "mobile-br-kc-internal"
}

### mobile-app-co (auth0) → account-service
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-co",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "mobile-co-auth0-client"
}

### internal-backoffice (keycloak) → all proxies
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "internal-backoffice",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "backoffice-kc-client"
}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "internal-backoffice",
  "proxyName": "billing-service",
  "audience": "backoffice-kc-client"
}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "internal-backoffice",
  "proxyName": "notification-service",
  "audience": "backoffice-kc-client"
}

### ============================================================
### 6. Create Rules with Validations
### ============================================================

### Rule: account-service + auth0 (jsonPath for auth0 JWT structure)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "idpName": "auth0",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/accounts/{msisdn}/balance",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.country",
      "validation": "equals"
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "level": 2,
      "paramName": "msisdn",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.aL",
      "validation": "contains",
      "enrichment": {
        "conditionJsonPath": "$.allAc",
        "conditionEquals": false,
        "endpoint": "/users/me",
        "domainFrom": "jwtIssuer",
        "responseJsonPath": "$.accountDetail.subscriptions[*].msisdn",
        "cacheTtlSeconds": 300
      }
    }
  ]
}

### Rule: account-service + keycloak (different jsonPaths!)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "idpName": "keycloak",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/accounts/{msisdn}/balance",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.realm_access.country",
      "validation": "equals"
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "level": 2,
      "paramName": "msisdn",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.realm_access.accounts",
      "validation": "contains"
    }
  ]
}
